WHAT = {"id": "what", "h1": "WHAT is <b>TIMECAPSULE</b>", "foot": "What is TimeCapsule", "blocks": [
 ("lead", "TimeCapsule is a digital place built around a different relationship with technology - one that uses its possibilities without letting its logic determine how we think, communicate and relate to the world."),
 ("p", "Rather than prioritising speed, efficiency and endless content, it makes room for reflection, dialogue and sustained human participation. People can start discussions, share experiences and ideas, raise questions and challenge perspectives."),
 ("p", "Through repeated participation, trust develops, relationships take shape and ideas evolve."),
 ("p", "At its heart is the understanding that knowledge is more than information: it emerges through human experience, reflection and dialogue."),
 ("p", "Encountering different perspectives deepens our understanding of ourselves, our societies and the world we inhabit."),
 ("p", "TimeCapsule preserves this experience as a lasting record of ideas, knowledge and discussions, together with the contexts they emerge from. Each contribution carries its history and authorship, and the possibility of meaningful exchange. Together, they form an evolving human imprint: an inheritance that future generations can encounter, question and build upon."),
 ("lead", "Technology serves human expression rather than replacing it. TimeCapsule is a shared human space where people meet, think, communicate and develop understanding together, preserving what each generation has to share for those who follow."),
]}

HOW = {"id": "how", "h1": "HOW to use <b>TIMECAPSULE</b>", "foot": "How to use TimeCapsule", "blocks": [
 ("lead", "TimeCapsule gives people the space and tools to develop ideas, connect around common interests and build communities through active participation. Shared interests and exchanged perspectives create, over time, a sense of belonging."),
 ("p", "Its environment combines human interaction with AI capabilities. AI tools help people follow discussions, discover relevant contributions, overcome language barriers, organise shared knowledge and prepare activities."),
 ("p", "This makes participation more accessible and collaboration easier, while judgement, creativity and initiative remain with people."),
 ("p", "Within TimeCapsule, people can:"),
 ("ul", [
   ["Host and participate:", "Organise and take part in live discussions, talks, lectures and workshops to exchange knowledge, explore ideas and learn from one another."],
   ["Turn ideas into shared projects:", "Connect with others, discover common ground, develop initiatives and put collective ideas into practice."],
   ["Preserve and pass on knowledge:", "Build a lasting record of ideas, experiences and discussions, with authorship and original context intact, so that future generations can revisit it and build upon it."]]),
]}

WHY = {"id": "why", "h1": "WHY to use <b>TIMECAPSULE</b>", "foot": "Why to use TimeCapsule", "blocks": [
 ("lead", "Technology has changed not only how we communicate, but the conditions under which we think, learn, work and relate to one another. Artificial intelligence is accelerating this change, increasingly taking part in activities once shaped by human judgement, creativity and experience. The question is no longer what technology can do, but what place we want it to have in our lives, and what we risk losing when its capabilities begin to define our purposes."),
 ("p", "TimeCapsule is a place where humans meet through technology, not a place where technology simulates the presence of humans. What is disappearing is not connectivity, but the human presence that gives connectivity its meaning."),
 ("p", "We can exchange more content without gaining understanding, communicate more often without building deeper relationships, and access vast information without acquiring knowledge. More communication does not automatically mean more meaningful participation."),
 ("p", "AI can extend human capabilities by generating answers, processing information and performing cognitive tasks. But producing an answer is not the same as understanding why a question matters."),
 ("lead", "Within TimeCapsule, AI assists people and never impersonates them: members are real people, not bots, and human participation is never replaced by artificial activity. Human judgement, responsibility and experience remain central."),
]}

EXISTS = {"id": "exists", "h1": "WHY <b>TIMECAPSULE</b> exists", "foot": "Why TimeCapsule exists", "blocks": [
 ("lead", "TimeCapsule emerges from the need for a digital environment that is safe, respectful and built around genuine participation, where trust, privacy and mutual respect allow people to express themselves and engage with different perspectives. Safety is essential, because meaningful communication cannot develop without a sense of security. Within it, sustained conversations, shared learning, communities and collective creation can grow."),
 ("p", "Ideas also deserve continuity. They should not disappear into the constant flow of digital content; their authorship, history and context should stay accessible for others to revisit, question and develop."),
 ("lead", "The purpose is not simply to connect more people or produce more content. It is to create a digital environment where technology serves human connection, shared knowledge and collective creation, while preserving the freedom, dignity and safety of the people who give it meaning."),
]}

MANIFESTO = {"id": "manifesto", "h1": "TIMECAPSULE <b>MANIFESTO</b><span class=\"sub\">We believe</span>", "foot": "TimeCapsule manifesto", "blocks": [
 ("bel", [
  "We believe technology should serve human life, not define its purposes. It can remain a means, without becoming the horizon within which everything acquires its meaning.",
  "We believe technological progress should expand human possibilities without reducing human existence to productivity, efficiency, calculation or measurable performance.",
  "We believe intelligence is more than the capacity to process information or produce answers. Human thought requires experience, imagination, interpretation, independent judgement and the freedom to question.",
  "We believe knowledge develops through observation, dialogue, disagreement, reflection and the encounter of different perspectives. Its value lies not only in what we know, but in how we come to understand.",
  "We believe communication is more than the transmission of content. It requires attention, reciprocity, trust and a willingness to encounter others.",
  "We believe participation must be active and meaningful. People should remain contributors to the knowledge, ideas and decisions that shape their shared world, rather than passive consumers of automated outputs.",
  "We believe communities grow through the continued involvement of their members. Through shared experiences, conversations and collective initiatives, people develop relationships, mutual understanding and the capacity to create together.",
  "We believe artificial intelligence should help people communicate, explore ideas, overcome barriers, organise knowledge and collaborate, extending human capabilities without replacing human judgement, initiative, authorship or responsibility.",
  "We believe human knowledge and experience deserve to be preserved, with their authorship, history and context intact, so that future generations can question and build upon them."]),
 ("lead", "We stand for a digital environment in which technology brings human possibilities closer to fulfilment: where people participate rather than merely consume, understand rather than simply process, create together rather than produce in isolation, and build relationships that give meaning to the world they share."),
]}

ANTIDOTE = {"id": "antidote", "h1": "<b>TIMECAPSULE</b>: An Antidote", "foot": "TimeCapsule: An Antidote", "blocks": [
 ("h2", "Against isolation and alienation"),
 ("p", "We are more connected than ever, and yet more alone. Connectivity gives contact, not presence. We exchange more content without gaining understanding, and communicate more often without building deeper relationships."),
 ("p", "TimeCapsule is a place where people meet through technology, not where technology simulates their presence. Members are real people, not bots. Through repeated participation, trust develops, relationships take shape and belonging grows. Alienation does not end through more content. It ends when someone listens, answers and remembers you. Where trust matters most, protected spaces keep that continuity private and secure."),
 ("h2", "Against the death of the internet"),
 ("p", "Every day, bots and agents produce most of what the internet contains. Words multiply, but fewer of them have anyone behind them. We can no longer tell who is speaking, or whether anyone is listening. What is dying is not the network but the presence that once gave it meaning."),
 ("p", "TimeCapsule does not compete with this flood. It restores what the flood erased: a human voice that can be trusted to be human. AI assists but never impersonates, so what people read is written by people, and what they say is heard by people. Here the internet can again be a shared human space."),
 ("h2", "For the preservation of the human imprint"),
 ("p", "Most of what we say online is lost within days, detached from its author, its context and the conversation that produced it. Ideas disappear into the constant flow of content."),
 ("p", "TimeCapsule preserves human experience as a lasting record, with each contribution carrying its history, authorship and context. A conversation does not end when it is over: it can be revisited, questioned and developed further. Together, these contributions form an evolving human imprint, an inheritance that future generations can encounter, question and build upon. In an age when machines can generate answers without limit, what deserves to be kept is the human experience from which questions arise."),
]}

FAQ = {"id": "faq", "h1": "<b>TIMECAPSULE</b>: Common Questions", "foot": "TimeCapsule: Common Questions", "blocks": [
 ("q", "1. Is TimeCapsule an LLM?"),
 ("p", "No. TimeCapsule is not an AI model and does not try to answer your questions for you. It is a place where people meet, and AI plays a supporting role within it."),
 ("p", "<i>Why use it when AI platforms can already perform so many tasks?</i> AI platforms are built to produce answers. TimeCapsule is built for what answers cannot supply: experience, disagreement, and the understanding that emerges when real people think together. Producing an answer is not the same as understanding why a question matters. Here, AI helps you follow discussions, find relevant contributions and overcome language barriers, while the thinking, judgement and authorship stay with people. Every member is a real person, and human participation is never replaced by artificial activity."),
 ("q", "2. Is TimeCapsule another social media platform?"),
 ("p", "No. It shares the idea of connecting people, but not the logic behind most social media. TimeCapsule does not prioritize speed, endless content or constant activity. It is organized around sustained conversation, shared interests and communities that grow through continued participation."),
 ("p", "<i>Why use it instead of conventional social media?</i> Conventional platforms help us exchange more content without gaining understanding or building deeper relationships. TimeCapsule is designed for the opposite: trust that develops through repeated participation, discussions that evolve over time, and a space that is safe, respectful and private enough for people to express themselves openly. Ideas also do not vanish into a feed. Each contribution keeps its authorship, history and context, so it can be revisited, questioned and developed further."),
 ("q", "3. Is TimeCapsule another Zoom?"),
 ("p", "No. Video conferencing tools connect people for a meeting, and when the call ends, little remains. TimeCapsule does offer live discussions, talks, lectures and workshops, but they are one part of a continuing space rather than isolated events."),
 ("p", "<i>Why use it instead of Zoom?</i> Because what happens in a live session does not end with it. Conversations are preserved with their context and authorship, and participants can return to them, continue them and build on them. Communities form around shared interests and continue between sessions. AI tools help with preparation, language barriers and organizing shared knowledge, which makes hosting and joining easier without replacing the people involved."),
 ("q", "4. Is TimeCapsule another TED or TEDx?"),
 ("p", "No. A TED talk is a one-directional format: a speaker presents and an audience listens. TimeCapsule is built on active participation, where people remain contributors rather than passive consumers."),
 ("p", "<i>Why use TimeCapsule?</i> Anyone can host a talk, lecture or workshop, but the talk is where the exchange begins, not where it ends. Audiences can ask questions, challenge perspectives and respond, and the discussion continues over time. Ideas can also grow into shared projects, as people find common ground and put collective ideas into practice. Everything is kept as a lasting record, so that future generations can encounter, question and build upon it."),
 ("q", "5. Is TimeCapsule another space for academics to present their research?"),
 ("p", "TimeCapsule offers researchers a place to present their work and discuss it in depth with an engaged community, not only with those in their own field or institution."),
 ("p", "<i>Why use TimeCapsule?</i> It offers dialogue over broadcast: researchers can present findings in live talks, lectures or workshops, then continue the conversation with questions, disagreement and different perspectives. AI tools help overcome language barriers, so research can be shared and discussed beyond a single language community. Each contribution keeps its history, authorship and original context, so research, and the discussion around it, can be revisited and developed further. Researchers can find common ground with others and turn ideas into shared projects. Academics can also export the transcript of their video paper and use it to create content, such as articles, summaries or teaching material. Knowledge and discussions are preserved as a lasting record for future generations to build upon, in a trusted environment where members are real people in a safe, respectful space and privacy and mutual respect matter."),
 ("q", "6. Is TimeCapsule another LinkedIn?"),
 ("p", "No. LinkedIn is built around professional profiles: who you are, where you have worked and what you have achieved. TimeCapsule is built around how people think and take part."),
 ("p", "<i>Why use TimeCapsule instead of LinkedIn?</i> On TimeCapsule, a member's interests, participation and approaches become visible through what they actually contribute: the questions they raise, the perspectives they bring and the way they engage with others. Their ability to grasp things, to understand, interpret and respond, can be seen in the discussions they take part in rather than claimed in a profile. Because each contribution keeps its authorship, history and context, this record builds over time through sustained participation. It lets people meet through shared interests and the quality of their thinking, and build relationships and communities that grow from real exchange."),
 ("q", "7. Can TimeCapsule hold existing communities and private relationships?"),
 ("p", "Yes. TimeCapsule is not only for public talks and open discussion. It can also preserve communities and personal relationships that already exist, and give them a place to continue over time."),
 ("p", "<i>Why use TimeCapsule?</i> A support community such as AA can keep meeting in one place, with its history and continuity intact. A psychoanalysis session can take place privately, and the relationship between analyst and patient has a space they can return to at any time. Or something simpler: a book club that meets once a month, or old university friends now living in different countries, can keep their table and pick up the conversation where they left off. Such spaces are private and protected with extreme security measures, so that trust, which these relationships depend on, is never put at risk. The same environment can hold an open talk and a protected conversation: public where people want to share, private where people need to be safe."),
]}

FULL = [WHAT, HOW, WHY, EXISTS, MANIFESTO, ANTIDOTE, FAQ]
